{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789796080,"nonce":"5g3dNM3pLkvOioD9xtfkk6xletY=","title":"LLVM: a phi of an aggregate held by reference was a phi of struct values","message":"The LLVM backend translated a phi typed as a multi-field struct into an\nLLVM phi of the struct type, while its incomings were addresses (a list\nheader parameter, a box read, a malloc); using the phi as a pointer\npanicked (\"Found StructValue ... expected PointerValue\") in the promoter\nthread. nqueens' `place` reached this once its calls were few enough for\nthe LLVM tier to accept it, and the promotion was lost each time.\n\nFix: a phi whose type `is_held_by_reference` is a phi of addresses, and\nan incoming that is a struct value is spilled to a frame slot in its\npredecessor; the reverse (an address into a phi of values) is read\nthrough. This follows the bitcast rule (3bf5370); the full aggregate\nconvention is e1efccb / e756498.","files":null}]}